From: OpenGrad <https://github.com/arrogance231/OpenGrad>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] examples/llama: derive the QNN cache shape from a layer that has a KV cache

`_to_edge_and_lower_llama` builds the `TagQuantIO` cache shape from
`model.layers[0].attention`, assuming layer 0 is a KV-cache attention module:

    atten = builder_exported_to_edge.model.layers[0].attention
    cache_shape = torch.Size(
        (atten.max_batch_size, atten.max_context_len, atten.n_kv_heads, atten.head_dim)
    )

That assumption does not hold for hybrid models. Qwen3.5 interleaves Gated DeltaNet
("linear_attention") and gated full attention, and `layer_types[0]` is `linear_attention` — a
block carrying recurrent state and no KV cache at all. The export fails with:

    AttributeError: 'AttentionGatedDeltaNet' object has no attribute 'max_context_len'

Selecting the first attention module that actually has a cache is both correct for homogeneous
models (layer 0 still wins) and correct for hybrids.

Note this fixes the crash, not the semantics: the resulting `cache_shape` describes only the
full-attention KV cache, and a hybrid model's recurrent-state I/O remains untagged for
quantization. A complete fix would tag both.

Applies to: pytorch/executorch @ df6147afadf106a0ef3a74f65d80b5c589e63e44

---
 examples/models/llama/export_llama_lib.py | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/examples/models/llama/export_llama_lib.py b/examples/models/llama/export_llama_lib.py
--- a/examples/models/llama/export_llama_lib.py
+++ b/examples/models/llama/export_llama_lib.py
@@ -1534,7 +1534,18 @@ def _to_edge_and_lower_llama(
-        atten = builder_exported_to_edge.model.layers[0].attention
+        # This derives a KV-cache shape for TagQuantIO, but layer 0 is not guaranteed to have a
+        # KV cache. Qwen3.5 is hybrid: layer_types[0] is "linear_attention", a Gated DeltaNet
+        # block with recurrent state and no cache, so layers[0].attention has no
+        # max_context_len/n_kv_heads/head_dim. Take the first attention that does.
+        atten = next(
+            (
+                layer.attention
+                for layer in builder_exported_to_edge.model.layers
+                if hasattr(layer.attention, "max_context_len")
+            ),
+            builder_exported_to_edge.model.layers[0].attention,
+        )
         if use_qnn_sha:
             cache_shape = torch.Size(
                 (atten.max_batch_size, atten.max_context_len, atten.head_dim)
             )
